  "title": "Qt: Use QFontDialog::MonospaceFonts for the monospace font pref",
  "description": "The prefs.gui_font_name preference has always supposed to be a\nmonospaced font, and now the FontManager enforces that. Only\nshow monospaced fonts in the QFontDialog, under the principle\nthat it's better to present the user with appropriate choices\nrather than allow the user to select a proportional font that\nwill then be silently swapped for a monospace font anyway.\n\nNote that this option might not have any effect on macOS (since\nthe native dialog is used by default, though that can be turned\noff.) It also won't work with the GTK3 dialog on Linux until\n6.12.0:\nhttps://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/544aa70c93cbf52c3b2b59801cb1c423e8e18275\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
